# Dark background text contrast

When placing text on a black, near-black, or otherwise dark background (`#111`, `#0d1b2a`, dark gradients, etc.), use light text so it remains readable.

## Rules

- Body copy on dark backgrounds: `color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85)` or `#fff`
- Secondary / muted copy on dark backgrounds: `color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.65)` minimum
- Headings on dark backgrounds: `#fff` or very high-opacity white
- Emphasis (`strong`, `em`) on dark backgrounds: stay at full white or a light accent — never dark gray or `var(--ink-soft)`

## Examples

```css
/* ✅ GOOD — dark panel */
.feed-data-window {
  background: #111;
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
}

/* ❌ BAD — dark panel with default body text color */
.dark-panel {
  background: #111;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}
```

Before shipping UI on dark sections, check default text tokens (`--ink`, `--ink-soft`) are not reused without a light override.
